well we often see images of deadly  crashes on our roads just like the  tragedy that unfolded in north las vegas  but we rarely see the emotional toll on  victims families years later especially  on children left behind it is a story 8  news now has been following in the  i-teams vanessa murphy has this  exclusive story from a perspective we  don't often hear about a child left  behind because of the crime  kayden mcginnis was two years old when  he was in this car with his mother and  two of her friends on halloween night in  2013. drunk driver leonard walker caused  this crash kaiden's mother savannah who  was just 17 was killed do you remember  her or  no  kaden is now 10 years old his  grandmother julie mcginnis was raising  him after the crash but in 2018 she  passed away from cancer he said love you  mama now kayden lives with his aunt  uncle and their six children i don't  even know who i am anymore  and i try to stay strong for my kids and  for him the most brianna cerrados admits  she is struggling after the loss of her  sister and her mother and she feels  justice hasn't been served it kills me  to know that i caused this through a  deal walker pleaded guilty to a felony  charge of driving under the influence  and causing death he received a sentence  of seven to 20 years this is the little  boy that will never see his mother again  in december of 2019 he was released on  residential confinement think house  arrest brianna says there wasn't much of  an effort to notify her then in august  of 2020 walker asked for parole i would  never do it again the 8 news now i-team  requested video of the hearing from the  parole board we were told there were  technical difficulties and we were  provided video with poor quality  i'm still trying to live with what i did  and decision i made  and to the victims i'm still i'm very  sorry  and i i really really hope you can  forgive me so i can really start to  forgive myself walker's girlfriend made  a plea too every day our daughter asks  if he can take her to the park  and i just ask for your consideration in  granting his pearl so we can finally  give our daughter what she's been asking  for and then i can't say that i forgive  him and i'm probably the most forgiving  person ever rihanna's turn and my mom  said that when she got the phone call at  9 19 p.m  with the news about my sister she died  at 9 19 p.m  and as i sat down riding this last night  i realized a big part of me died too she  asked for walker to serve the remainder  of his sentence behind bars to go 85  miles an hour i want you guys to  understand my sister was internally  decapitated  and they found her with her arms thrown  over my nephew  the only one not hurt because  and all i could think  every day is what were her last words  how scared was she how scared was he  i play these images in my head and it  doesn't go away kayden was at that  hearing the dude who killed my mom  he was like right there it's been really  hard for me  i don't even know what it's like to even  have a mom the next month the family  received this letter leonard walker was  granted parole  the 29 year old sentence is set to  finish completely this june according to  the department of corrections what i  would like is him to serve a life  sentence like we're serving she says  holidays especially halloween are a  painful time for their family kaden  didn't speak for more than a year after  the crash due to ptsd  and now he sits trying to explain what  happened to his mom to other kids at  school is a challenge  because people ask about it i tell them  about it they don't believe anything  vanessa murphy everything he knows has  been taken live local now
 

